INT. ROLLER RINK - TEMPORARY COURTROOM - DAY

The county courthouse flooded in March. Now a folding table stands on the maple skating floor, and a disco ball hangs dead above it. Rental skates hang on a wall rack behind the bench.

NADIA BRZEZINSKI, 40s, public defender, sorts papers into two stacks. Her suit is good but the shoes are sneakers. She looks at the door twice.

A YOUNG MAN in a borrowed suit sits across from her. The sleeves cover his knuckles. He is picking at the cuff.

YOUNG MAN
They said it'd be at the courthouse.

NADIA
It's under four feet of water.

YOUNG MAN
Right.

He nods. He keeps nodding a moment too long.

NADIA
You didn't wear the tie I told you to.

YOUNG MAN
It's in the car.

NADIA
Is the car here?

He looks at the exit sign. She watches him look.

NADIA (CONT'D)
What's your name? Say it for me. The way you'll say it to her.

YOUNG MAN
Tobias Wren.

NADIA
Again. Slower.

TOBIAS
Tobias Wren.

She slides a pen across the table. He doesn't take it. She leaves it there.

NADIA
The state's offer expires at ten. It's nine fifty.

TOBIAS
My mom said I shouldn't sign anything.

NADIA
Your mom isn't here.

TOBIAS
She's in the lot.

Nadia stops sorting. She puts both hands flat on the table.

NADIA
Go get her.

Tobias stands. Sits back down. Stands again. Walks halfway to the door and turns around.

TOBIAS
I'll sign it.

NADIA
Don't do it because I said "go get her."

He picks up the pen. His hand is steady now, steadier than hers.

The side door bangs open. JUDGE FAUSTINA OYELOWO-MARSH, 60s, robe over a cardigan, enters on rental skates and rolls to a stop at the bench. Nobody laughs.

JUDGE OYELOWO-MARSH
Counsel. Mr. Wren. We are on the record.

Tobias holds the pen above the page. Nadia takes it out of his fingers, gently, and caps it.

NADIA
Your Honor, we need ten more minutes.

JUDGE OYELOWO-MARSH
You have two.

Nadia nods. Tobias, very quietly, starts to untie his shoes.
